    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter September 5th with a clear emphasis on power and high-leverage counting stats, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.22). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary engine against the right-handed arm of Gray, benefiting from a significant 14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against Lugo. Among our outfielders, **Heliot Ramos** (63.60) stands out as a strong play; despite a slight park disadvantage, he gains nearly 20% in efficiency from the SP skill profile of Ray, positioning him as a high-floor start today.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Wade Meckler** (41.54), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Wade Meckler** offers a solid situational profile against Ashcraft, his raw projected efficiency didn't quite eclipse the cumulative utility of **Henry Bolte** (49.75) or **Jackson Merrill** (53.53). We are closely monitoring the matchup for **Luis Lara** (59.60), who is positioned to exploit Abbott\u2019s high xERA of 5.02. Caution is advised with **Liam Hicks** (41.19) and **Dominic Smith** (41.89), both of whom are facing elite arms in deGrom and Wheeler, respectively; while they provide structural depth, their scoring ceilings are compressed by the caliber of the opposing pitching. We continue to manage our remaining roster depth\u2014including **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Franklin Arias**\u2014as we navigate the final stretch of the season and prioritize the scarcity of stolen base production.",
